---
import Adr from "../components/Adr.astro";
import Diagram from "../components/Diagram.astro";
import Excerpt from "../components/Excerpt.astro";
import Layer from "../components/Layer.astro";
import Layout from "../components/Layout.astro";
import Path from "../components/Path.astro";
import Routes from "../components/Routes.astro";
import Rule from "../components/Rule.astro";
import Sequence from "../components/Sequence.astro";

const AM = "server/src/iki_server/amounts";
const ST = "server/src/iki_server/storage";
const LIMS = "plugins/example_lims/types";

const boxes = [
  { id: "decl", x: 20, y: 30, w: 190, h: 60, label: "Type declarations", sub: "storage: and amount:" },
  { id: "units", x: 250, y: 30, w: 190, h: 60, label: "UCUM units", sub: "exact conversions" },
  { id: "places", x: 480, y: 30, w: 190, h: 60, label: "Plugin places", sub: "freezer, rack, box, tube" },
  { id: "receive", x: 710, y: 30, w: 190, h: 60, label: "Receiving", sub: "receive_into, receipts" },
  { id: "eligible", x: 20, y: 150, w: 190, h: 60, label: "Eligibility", sub: "holds, draw guards" },
  { id: "ledger", x: 250, y: 150, w: 190, h: 60, label: "Amount ledger", sub: "append-only movements", strong: true },
  { id: "place", x: 480, y: 150, w: 190, h: 60, label: "Place", sub: "container, row, column" },
  { id: "events", x: 710, y: 150, w: 190, h: 60, label: "Location ledger", sub: "append-only events", strong: true },
  { id: "balance", x: 250, y: 270, w: 190, h: 60, label: "Balance", sub: "one row; never below 0" },
  { id: "graph", x: 20, y: 270, w: 190, h: 60, label: "Graph edges", sub: "aliquot, transfer, used" },
  { id: "moves", x: 480, y: 270, w: 190, h: 60, label: "Bulk moves", sub: "preview, then commit" },
  { id: "counts", x: 710, y: 270, w: 190, h: 60, label: "Counts", sub: "plan_revision pinned" },
];
const edges = [
  { from: "decl", to: "eligible", label: "guards" },
  { from: "units", to: "ledger", label: "converts" },
  { from: "eligible", to: "ledger" },
  { from: "ledger", to: "balance", label: "same transaction" },
  { from: "ledger", to: "graph", label: "trigger" },
  { from: "places", to: "place", label: "instances" },
  { from: "events", to: "place" },
  { from: "moves", to: "events", label: "one operation" },
  { from: "counts", to: "events", label: "on completion" },
  { from: "receive", to: "events", label: "places" },
  ];

const H = {
  short: "Where material is, and how much is left",
  how: "From a type's declaration to ledgers of what moved",
  example: "A reagent delivery, a tube drawn for an assay, and a rack moved",
  rules: "Amounts, draws, places, moves, receipts and counts",
  ref: "Routes, code and decisions",
};
const toc = [
  { id: "short", label: H.short },
  { id: "how", label: H.how },
  { id: "move-seq", label: "A bulk move, previewed then committed" },
  { id: "example", label: H.example },
  { id: "rules", label: H.rules },
  { id: "ref", label: H.ref },
];
---

<Layout toc={toc}>
  <Layer n={1} title={H.short}>
    <p>
      Iki itself declares no freezers or tubes: plugins say which types hold others, in what grid,
      and which types have an amount in what unit. The server keeps two append-only ledgers: one of
      amounts, where every draw, transfer, split and adjustment is a movement with the balance after
      it, and one of locations, where every placement, move and hand-over is an event. The current
      balance and the current place are single rows updated in the same transaction. Moves of many
      records are previewed, then committed all or none.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>A record's amount is a ledger of what moved (<Adr n="0139" />).</li>
      <li>Where material is, and how it's received, moved and counted (<Adr n="0180" />).</li>
      <li>Received packs go straight into storage (<Adr n="0190" />).</li>
      <li>Commit the plan that was reviewed (<Adr n="0207" />).</li>
    </ul>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={2} title={H.how}>
    <Diagram id="stor" title="Declarations, the two ledgers, and what writes to them" width={920} height={350} boxes={boxes} edges={edges}>
      <div slot="decl">
        <p>
          <code>storage:</code> says what a type holds, its grid, its barcode field and which
          operations need a scan. <code>amount:</code> gives the unit, an optional concentration, and
          the records whose guards a draw also follows (<Adr n={[139, 180]} />).
        </p>
        <p><Path p="spec/src/iki_spec/model.py" sym="class Storage:" />, <Path p="spec/src/iki_spec/model.py" sym="class Amount:" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="units">
        <p>
          An amount's unit must add up: a volume, a mass, or a count; percentages and parts per
          million are refused. Conversions are exact fractions, from Iki's own UCUM parser (<Adr
            n="0139"
          />).
        </p>
        <p><Path p="spec/src/iki_spec/validate.py" sym="def _adds_up(" />, <Path p="spec/src/iki_spec/units/__init__.py" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="places">
        <p>
          The example LIMS plugin's freezer holds shelves, a shelf holds racks and boxes, a rack is a
          5 × 4 grid of boxes, and a box's grid comes from its own fields (<Adr n="0180" />).
        </p>
        <p><Path p={`${LIMS}/freezer.yaml`} />, <Path p={`${LIMS}/rack.yaml`} />, <Path p={`${LIMS}/box.yaml`} /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="receive">
        <p>
          An action that creates with <code>receive_into</code> opens each new record's amount and
          places it, in the run's transaction, with the run as the move's operation. Receipts against
          a request are checked line by line (<Adr n={[180, 190]} />).
        </p>
        <p><Path p="server/src/iki_server/runs/results.py" sym="def _place_received(" />, <Path p={`${ST}/receipts.py`} /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="eligible">
        <p>
          Before taking material: is the record in a state that holds its amount, do its draw guards
          pass, and those of the records it follows, and is there enough (<Adr n={[139, 162]} />).
        </p>
        <p><Path p={`${AM}/services.py`} sym="def _taking(" />, <Path p={`${AM}/eligibility.py`} /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="ledger">
        <p>
          Each movement keeps its kind, the signed change and the balance after it, what was asked
          for in its own unit, the counterpart, what it was used in, the person, agent and reason.
          Triggers refuse UPDATE, DELETE and TRUNCATE (<Adr n={[25, 139]} />).
        </p>
        <p><Path p={`${AM}/models.py`} sym="class Movement(" />, <Path p="server/src/iki_server/plugins/operations.py" sym="class AppendOnly(" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="place">
        <p>
          One row per record. One record per position is a deferred unique constraint, so a swap
          commits as one change; a trigger checks each position against the container's grid (<Adr
            n="0180"
          />).
        </p>
        <p><Path p={`${ST}/models.py`} sym="class Place(" />, <Path p={`${ST}/migrations/0001_initial.py`} sym="iki_storage_place_in_grid()" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="events">
        <p>
          Every placement, move, removal, check-out and hand-over is an event with where from and
          where to, audited as <code>storage.moved</code> and sent to webhooks (<Adr n="0180" />).
        </p>
        <p><Path p={`${ST}/models.py`} sym="class Event(" />, <Path p={`${ST}/services.py`} sym='"storage.moved"' /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="balance">
        <p>
          The current amount is a stored row, the ledger's last balance, not a sum taken on read. The
          database refuses a negative one. Its last change time is the balance's revision (<Adr
            n="0139"
          />).
        </p>
        <p><Path p={`${AM}/models.py`} sym='name="iki_amount_not_negative"' /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="graph">
        <p>
          A statement trigger on movements adds lineage edges: aliquot, transfer and used, so a
          draw's experiment shows upstream of the tube (<Adr n={[123, 139]} />).
        </p>
        <p><Path p="server/src/iki_server/graph/sql.py" sym="MOVEMENTS = (" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="moves">
        <p>
          Up to 1,536 moves with one reason, all or none, under one operation. The same endpoint
          previews, changing nothing and naming the plan it shows, and commits that plan only as
          shown (<Adr n={[180, 207]} />).
        </p>
        <p><Path p="server/src/iki_server/api/storage.py" sym="if payload.preview:" />, <Path p={`${ST}/services.py`} sym="def move(" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="counts">
        <p>
          Receipts and counts carry a <code>plan_revision</code>; editing one advances it, and
          completing a count is refused if anything moved in or out since it started (<Adr
            n={[180, 207]}
          />).
        </p>
        <p><Path p={`${ST}/reconciliations.py`} sym="def _advance_plan(" />, <Path p={`${ST}/reconciliations.py`} sym="storage.events_since(container, reconciliation.started_at)" /></p>
      </div>
    </Diagram>

    <h3 id="move-seq">A bulk move, previewed then committed</h3>
    <Sequence
      id="move-dg"
      title="Moving a rack to another shelf before a defrost"
      width={900}
      actors={[
        { id: "person", label: "Lab member" },
        { id: "app", label: "Web app", sub: "MoveDialog" },
        { id: "api", label: "API", sub: "/storage/moves" },
        { id: "svc", label: "storage.services" },
        { id: "db", label: "Postgres" },
      ]}
      steps={[
        { id: "pick", from: "person", to: "app", label: "records, a destination scan, a reason" },
        { id: "preview", from: "app", to: "api", label: "POST, preview: true" },
        { id: "plan", from: "api", to: "svc", label: "plan(): positions and problems, no locks" },
        { id: "review", from: "app", to: "person", label: "each move and problem, for review", dashed: true },
        { id: "commit", from: "app", to: "api", label: "the same items and the plan, preview: false" },
        { id: "lock", from: "svc", to: "db", label: "lock records and containers, in id order" },
        { id: "replan", from: "svc", to: "svc", label: "plan() again; not the plan shown: 409" },
        { id: "apply", from: "svc", to: "db", label: "places and events, one operation; clash check" },
      ]}
    >
      <div slot="pick"><p>The destination is resolved from its scan. Types that need a scan to move also ask for the records' own scans.</p><p><Path p="web/app/src/storage-ui.tsx" sym="export function MoveDialog(" /></p></div>
      <div slot="preview"><p>The request body names each record and where it goes, with or without a position.</p><p><Path p="server/src/iki_server/api/storage.py" sym="class MovesIn(" /></p></div>
      <div slot="plan"><p>When no position is given, the planner takes the next free one in the container's order.</p><p><Path p={`${ST}/services.py`} sym="def plan(" /></p></div>
      <div slot="review"><p>Nothing has changed yet. The preview also returns <code>plan</code>: a SHA-256 of each record, where it is, and the container and position it goes to.</p><p><Path p={`${ST}/services.py`} sym="def identify(" /></p></div>
      <div slot="commit"><p>The dialog sends back the plan it showed. An API caller may leave it out; then a position left empty is the next free one when the moves are made.</p><p><Path p="server/src/iki_server/api/storage.py" sym="plan: str | None = Field(" /></p></div>
      <div slot="lock"><p>A record whose location changed since it was read is refused.</p><p><Path p={`${ST}/services.py`} sym="def move(" /></p></div>
      <div slot="replan"><p>The plan is computed again under the locks. If it isn't the plan shown, because another placement took a position or a record moved meanwhile, nothing moves: 409 <code>moves_plan_changed</code> carries what the moves would do now, and the dialog shows what changed per record for a fresh confirmation. Otherwise a single problem refuses every move with 422 (<Adr n="0207" />).</p><p><Path p={`${ST}/services.py`} sym="raise PlanChanged(planned)" />, <Path p="web/app/src/storage-ui.tsx" sym='"moves_plan_changed"' /></p></div>
      <div slot="apply"><p>The deferred position constraint is checked before commit, so a clash refuses the whole move.</p><p><Path p={`${ST}/services.py`} sym="def _check_now(" /></p></div>
    </Sequence>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={3} title={H.example}>
    <p>
      A reagent order arrives. The <code>receive_delivery</code> action creates stock lots and puts
      them in storage as it records them; the lot type keeps its amount in millilitres, and a new lot
      starts in quarantine:
    </p>
    <Excerpt file="plugins/reagents/actions/receive_delivery.yaml" start="^effects:" />
    <p>
      Until QA releases it, only a QA sampling draw may take from the lot. Its draw guards, which any
      tube following the lot inherits:
    </p>
    <Excerpt file="plugins/lots/types/lot.yaml" start="^draw_guards:" />
    <p>
      Once QA has released the lot, a technician transfers 500 µL into a tube; the transfer converts exactly between the lot's mL and
      the tube's µL, or is refused. The tube's amount follows its lot and sample, and a draw needs a
      scan of the tube:
    </p>
    <Excerpt file={`${LIMS}/tube.yaml`} start="^amount:" />
    <Excerpt file={`${LIMS}/tube.yaml`} start="^storage:" />
    <p>The tube goes into a box, whose grid size comes from the box's own fields:</p>
    <Excerpt file={`${LIMS}/box.yaml`} start="^storage:" />
    <p>
      For an assay, a scientist draws 50 µL with <code>POST /api/v1/entities/&#123;tube&#125;/amount/draw</code>,
      naming the experiment it's used in and scanning the tube. The server locks the tube and the
      records it follows, checks the guards and the balance, appends a <code>drawn</code> movement
      with its purpose, and the graph gains a <code>used</code> edge from the tube to the experiment.
      Before a freezer is defrosted, the rack holding the box is moved to another shelf: a shelf has
      no grid, so nothing is allocated, and every box and tube in the rack keeps its place.
    </p>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={4} title={H.rules}>
    <div class="rules">
      <Rule title="Movement kinds and draw purposes" open>
        <Excerpt file={`${AM}/models.py`} start="^class MovementKind\(" />
        <p>
          A <code>drawn</code> movement must have a purpose and no other kind may; only a draw can
          name what it was used in. Both are database checks (<Path
            p={`${AM}/models.py`}
            sym='name="iki_amount_draw_purpose"'
          />).
        </p>
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="Concurrency and exact arithmetic">
        <p>
          Draws lock the records, in key order, then their amount rows; a second draw waits and sees
          what's left. Arithmetic runs at twice the stored precision (40 digits) with half-even
          rounding. Each change moves the balance's timestamp forward by at least a microsecond,
          because that timestamp is the balance's revision (<Adr n="0139" />, <Path
            p={`${AM}/services.py`}
            sym="def _lock_records("
          />).
        </p>
        <p>
          An adjustment needs a reason and the <code>If-Balance-Revision</code> header: without it,
          428; stale, 409 <code>stale_balance</code> (<Path p="server/src/iki_server/api/amounts.py" sym='alias="If-Balance-Revision"' />).
        </p>
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="Transfers, pools and lots">
        <p>
          Both sides of a transfer must be exact, or it's refused. Transferring into a record with a
          concentration rewrites the concentration as a revision, with the transfer as its reason. A
          type with <code>material:</code> takes material only of the same entity, and a locked record
          only material in its own state (<Adr n={[157, 162]} />, <Path
            p={`${AM}/services.py`}
            sym="def _pool("
          />, <Path p={`${AM}/services.py`} sym="def _what_it_takes(" />). A split makes at most 200
          aliquots.
        </p>
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="Bulk moves, as reviewed">
        <p>
          A preview names what it shows; confirming sends that name back, and the server compares it
          with the plan it computes under the moves' locks. A different well, source, container or
          order gives a different name. Problems and proofs aren't part of it, since they're checked
          again when the moves are made (<Adr n={[180, 207]} />).
        </p>
        <Excerpt file={`${ST}/services.py`} start="^def identify\(" />
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="Places, grids and the location ledger">
        <p>
          A container's shape is kept when it's first used, append-only, and checked to be a valid
          grid of at most 32 by 48 (<Adr n="0180" />, <Path
            p="spec/src/iki_spec/model.py"
            sym="GRID_POSITIONS = 1536"
          />).
        </p>
        <Excerpt file={`${ST}/models.py`} start="^class EventKind\(" />
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="Receipts, counts and stability pulls">
        <p>
          A request can have one open receipt. A stale receipt revision answers with the lines that
          changed. A count never passes an empty position to the planner, so it never allocates a
          slot of its own (<Adr n={[180, 207]} />, <Path p={`${ST}/models.py`} sym='name="iki_storage_receipt_one_open"' />).
          A stability pull draws once, from its assigned tube and lot, in its planned quantity (<Adr
            n="0193"
          />, <Path p={`${AM}/services.py`} sym="def _check_draw_target(" />).
        </p>
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="Where the ADRs and the code differ">
        <ul>
          <li>
            An adjustment's <code>If-Balance-Revision</code> requirement is in no ADR; <Adr n="0139" />
            asks only for a reason.
          </li>
          <li>
            <Adr n="0139" /> still says a location stays a field and containers aren't modelled;
            <Adr n="0180" /> changed that, and the example box's <code>location</code> field is marked
            removed.
          </li>
          <li>
            <Adr n="0180" />'s example freezer holds racks and boxes; the plugin adds a shelf between
            them.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </Rule>
    </div>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={5} title={H.ref}>
    <Routes tags={["storage"]} />
    <Routes tags={["amounts"]} />
    <div class="refs">
      <h3>Where</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><Path p={AM} />: the amount ledger, eligibility and stock</li>
        <li><Path p={ST} />: places, events, moves, receipts and counts</li>
        <li><Path p="spec/src/iki_spec/units" />: UCUM units</li>
        <li><Path p="web/app/src/storage-ui.tsx" />: the app's storage dialogs</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Decisions</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><Adr n="0139" title /></li>
        <li><Adr n="0157" title /></li>
        <li><Adr n="0162" title /></li>
        <li><Adr n="0180" title /></li>
        <li><Adr n="0190" title /></li>
        <li><Adr n="0193" title /></li>
        <li><Adr n="0207" title /></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </Layer>
</Layout>
